# vercel.json pins outputDirectory to the repo root, so WITHOUT this file every
# file here is served at a public URL. That is not theoretical: docs/, README.md,
# build.py, the design canvas and .env.example all answered 200.
#
# docs/ is the one that matters. The design spec is a dossier on the recipient —
# her age, her job, her city, quotes of things she has said, her dietary
# constraints — and it contains the line "for a reader who is explicitly wary of
# how much men know about her". Sitting it at a guessable path on the same domain
# as the invitation is the single thing most likely to undo the invitation.
#
# README.md is the second: it explains the No button's three dodges, the
# notification wiring and every joke, before she has met any of them.
#
# After deploying, verify. Anything but 404 means this file is not doing its job:
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://YOUR-DOMAIN/README.md
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://YOUR-DOMAIN/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-pigeon-garden-invite-design.md

# The spec and the brief. Never ship these.
docs/

# The art pipeline and its raw generated sources. Only the derived art-*.png at
# the repo root are actually used by the page.
assets/

# Every markdown file, README included.
*.md

# The design canvas and the local build/preview tooling. The site is static; none
# of this is needed at runtime.
*.dc.html
build.py
devserver.py
visual_refresh.py
preview_screens.py
garden.css
.local-review/
__pycache__/
tests/
pixel.html
build_pixel.py
build_kingdom.py
build_journey.py
journey.html
journey.css
journey.js
journey-data.js
scenery/
!vendor/ANIME-LICENSE.md

# Names the notification vars and carries a sample address. Nothing secret, but
# nothing anyone visiting the invitation needs either.
.env.example

# Vercel does not serve root dotfiles today, but do not depend on that. This file
# in particular describes exactly what it is hiding and where.
.gitignore
.vercelignore
.claude/
